<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Build Boundary From Tracks" GL-hosting dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormBuildBoundaryFromTracks`
    (FormBuildBoundaryFromTracks.cs + .Designer.cs + .resx, 831 lines). The operator (de)selects the
    field's saved tracks in a scrollable list beside a live OpenGL preview, nudges the active track's
    A/B ends (extend / shrink), auto-finds intersections, builds the trimmed boundary, then saves it.
    Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the current Windows Forms look, never
    a redesign: no new colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormBuildBoundaryFromTracks.Designer.cs:
      Text "Build Boundary From Tracks" -> Title (design-time; the code-behind assigns the localised
                                           gStr string at runtime, matching the sibling views).
      ClientSize 1008 x 729             -> Width="1008" Height="729" (1:1 WinForms-px -> Avalonia DIP,
                                           the convention used by every sibling GPS view).
      FormBorderStyle.None + custom 15px DarkGray OnPaint border, ControlBox=false
                                        -> a normal decorated, RESIZABLE window. The WinForms form was
                                           borderless ONLY so it could paint its own frame; with a
                                           decorated Avalonia window the OS supplies the frame and resize
                                           grips, so the custom border is intentionally NOT reproduced
                                           (it would double-frame). This matches the analogous resizable
                                           host dialog FormWebCamView, which is likewise decorated.
      (resizable preview)               -> CanResize="True" — the glControlPreview was Anchor
                                           Top|Bottom|Left|Right (it stretched), so the Avalonia GL host
                                           fills the left column and grows with the window.
      StartPosition CenterScreen, shown owned by FormGPS -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
      ShowInTaskbar = false             -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      BackColor Gainsboro               -> Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}" — the neutral
                                           chrome is themed to the App.axaml day/night palette (this
                                           file's only dependency) rather than hard-coding a WinForms
                                           colour, exactly like the sibling FormFieldDirView.

    GL-HOSTING (markup side only):
      The WinForms `glControlPreview` (OpenTK.GLControl, BackColor Black) is REPLACED by an empty host
      container `oglHost` (a Border). The code-behind constructs the cross-platform
      AvaloniaGeoViewport and inserts its exposed Control (`_viewport.View`) into oglHost at runtime.
      There is deliberately NO OpenTK.GLControl, NO Avalonia OpenGlControlBase, and NO AgOpenGPS.Controls
      reference in this markup — the GL control type is purely a code-behind concern (Pure Avalonia rule).
      oglHost keeps the source's Black backdrop so the surface reads correctly before/while the viewport
      attaches.

    TRACK LIST:
      The WinForms `flpTrackList` (a FlowLayoutPanel, FlowDirection TopDown, AutoScroll, Fixed3D border)
      of per-track CheckBoxes becomes a native `ScrollViewer` wrapping an `ItemsControl x:Name="flpTrackList"`.
      The code-behind populates it with one CheckBox per track (CreateTrackCheckbox in the source) and
      recolours them (green / gold-active / orange-deselected) exactly as before. The default ItemsControl
      panel is a vertical StackPanel, reproducing the TopDown flow. The ScrollViewer gives native
      touch/wheel scrolling, so the WinForms manual drag-scroll plumbing (StartDrag / DoDrag /
      FlpTrackList_Mouse* and the _lastDragEndTime debounce) is intentionally NOT ported. `lblList`
      (a TextBlock) is the list caption above it.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind (FormBuildBoundaryFromTracksView.axaml.cs,
    partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormBuildBoundaryFromTracksView : Window) owns ALL behaviour:
      * Code-behind dialog: NO DataContext, NO x:DataType, NO MVVM bindings — exactly like the sibling
        FormWebCamView / FormFieldDirView / FormInputDialogView. Every control is addressed imperatively
        by its x:Name.
      * Click handlers are NOT declared as XAML attributes here. They are attached PROGRAMMATICALLY in
        the code-behind to the named button fields (the faithful port of the WinForms designer's
        `this.btnX.Click += ...`), so this markup never depends on a specific handler-method name — the
        same convention documented on the sibling FormWebCamView.
      * The x:Names below MUST stay exactly as written; the code-behind references each by name:
        oglHost, flpTrackList, lblList, btnAutoFind, btnSelectPrevious, btnSelectNext, btnExtendBackward,
        btnShrinkA, btnShrinkB, btnExtendForward, btnResetPreview, btnBuildBoundary, btnSave, btnClose.
      * btnSave starts IsEnabled="False" (WinForms InitializeForm: btnSave.Enabled = false); the
        code-behind enables it once a boundary has been built (btnBuildBoundary_Click / BuildBoundary).

    THEME & ASSETS:
      All colours come from App.axaml's day/night ThemeDictionaries via {DynamicResource ...} so the live
      Light<->Dark switch is observed — no WinForms colours, no GDI namespaces. Button glyphs are served
      from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs — the same btnImages/ assets
      the other GPS Avalonia views consume. btnClose uses Cancel64.png and btnSave uses OK64.png (per this
      file's spec); the remaining buttons keep their original glyphs and text labels.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormBuildBoundaryFromTracksView"
        Title="Build Boundary From Tracks"
        Width="1008"
        Height="729"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <!--
        Flat, chrome-less image-above-text command buttons reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor = Transparent + TextImageRelation.ImageAboveText
        carried by every button in the designer: a centred 64px glyph with its caption beneath, and no
        button surface in any interaction state. The :pointerover / :pressed / :disabled template
        overrides suppress the Fluent hover / press / disabled fill that would otherwise box the glyph;
        the :disabled Opacity reproduces the greyed look WinForms gives a disabled Button.Image (e.g. the
        initially-disabled btnSave). The descendant TextBlock setter themes every caption to the day/night
        text brush and centres it under the glyph.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.trackButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="Width" Value="95" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="95" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.trackButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.trackButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.trackButton:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.trackButton:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.trackButton TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="TextAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,2,0,0" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Two columns reproduce the designer: the GL preview fills the left (glControlPreview was anchored
        on all four sides, so it stretches), the command panel occupies a fixed-width right column. An
        outer margin stands in for the WinForms 8px client inset.
    -->
    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="10">

        <!--
            Col 0 — GL preview host. EMPTY by design: the code-behind injects the AvaloniaGeoViewport's
            Control (`_viewport.View`) here at runtime. Black backdrop matches the WinForms
            glControlPreview.BackColor = Black and the GL ClearColor(Black) clear in the source.
        -->
        <Border x:Name="oglHost"
                Grid.Column="0"
                MinWidth="400"
                Background="Black" />

        <!--
            Col 1 — the command panel. Five rows mirror the designer's right-hand stack: list caption,
            the scrollable track list (fills the remaining height), then three button bands — track
            navigation, A/B end adjustment, and the final actions.
        -->
        <Grid Grid.Column="1"
              Width="430"
              Margin="12,0,0,0"
              RowDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto,Auto,Auto">

            <!-- lblList — list caption (WinForms Label, MS Sans Serif 15.75pt Bold -> ~21 DIP). Runtime
                 text is assigned by the code-behind; the design-time text mirrors the designer. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblList"
                       Grid.Row="0"
                       Text="(De)Select Tracks to use"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       FontSize="21"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Margin="0,0,0,8" />

            <!--
                Track list — the FlowLayoutPanel (TopDown, AutoScroll, Fixed3D) becomes a bordered
                ScrollViewer over an ItemsControl. The Fixed3D sunken edge is approximated by a 1px
                neutral border (the literal-hex approach used by the sibling FormFilePickerView). Native
                vertical scrolling replaces the WinForms manual drag-scroll. The code-behind fills
                flpTrackList with one CheckBox per track; the default vertical StackPanel item layout
                reproduces the TopDown flow, with a small inter-item gap.
            -->
            <Border Grid.Row="1"
                    BorderBrush="#FF7F7F7F"
                    BorderThickness="1"
                    Margin="0,0,0,8">
                <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                              HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
                    <ItemsControl x:Name="flpTrackList" Margin="4">
                        <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                            <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="4" />
                            </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                    </ItemsControl>
                </ScrollViewer>
            </Border>

            <!--
                Row 2 — track navigation band: Auto Find (find intersections), Previous / Next (cycle the
                active track). Designer: btnAutoFind (ABDraw), btnSelectPrevious (ArrowLeft),
                btnSelectNext (ArrowRight).
            -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Row="2"
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="6"
                        Margin="0,0,0,8">
                <Button x:Name="btnAutoFind"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Auto Find">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ABDraw.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Auto Find" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnSelectPrevious"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Previous track">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ArrowLeft.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Previous" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnSelectNext"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Next track">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ArrowRight.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Next" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--
                Row 3 — A/B end adjustment band. Designer order (left to right): btnExtendBackward
                ("Extend A", APlusPlusA), btnShrinkA ("Shrink A", APlusMinusA), btnShrinkB ("Shrink B",
                APlusMinusB), btnExtendForward ("Extend B", APlusPlusB).
            -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Row="3"
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="6"
                        Margin="0,0,0,8">
                <Button x:Name="btnExtendBackward"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Extend A">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/APlusPlusA.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Extend A" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnShrinkA"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Shrink A">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/APlusMinusA.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Shrink A" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnShrinkB"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Shrink B">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/APlusMinusB.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Shrink B" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnExtendForward"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Extend B">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/APlusPlusB.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Extend B" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

            <!--
                Row 4 — final action band. Designer order (left to right): btnResetPreview ("Reset",
                Reset_Default), btnBuildBoundary ("Build", Boundary), btnSave ("Save", OK64 — starts
                disabled), btnClose ("Close", Cancel64). btnSave / btnClose use the OK64 / Cancel64 glyphs
                per this file's spec.
            -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Row="4"
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="6">
                <Button x:Name="btnResetPreview"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Reset preview">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Reset_Default.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Reset" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnBuildBoundary"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Build boundary">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Boundary.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Build" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnSave"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        IsEnabled="False"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Save boundary">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Save" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnClose"
                        Classes="trackButton"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Close">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                               Width="50" Height="50" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        <TextBlock Text="Close" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
